        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(gateway): lock config mutation allowlist contract",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway `config.patch` / `config.apply` mutations are guarded by an allowlist, but the contract was not locked in tests. A regression could silently widen or narrow which config paths agents may change.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a focused contract test suite that exercises both the allowlist guard and the real `createGatewayTool().execute()` path for `config.patch` and `config.apply`, so future edits cannot drift without failing CI.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change for operators. Maintainers and contributors get a stable regression gate on gateway config mutation policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/gateway-tool-allowlist.contract.test.ts --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Gateway agent tool config mutations must reject protected paths and dangerous flags before RPC, and allow only allowlisted paths through `createGatewayTool` execution.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS (Darwin), Node.js v22.22.0.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/gateway-tool-allowlist.contract.test.ts --run --reporter=verbose`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/gateway-tool-allowlist.contract.test.ts --run --reporter=verbose\n ✓ gateway config mutation allowlist contract (12 tests)\n ✓ gateway tool config mutation execution path (4 tests)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** `createGatewayTool().execute()` with `config.patch` forwards allowlisted edits to RPC and rejects protected/dangerous paths before RPC; `config.apply` rejects protected wholesale replacements before RPC.\n- **What was not tested:** Live gateway RPC against a running gateway instance; contract tests mock the RPC client and exercise the production guard + tool execution path.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/gateway-tool-allowlist.contract.test.ts --run --reporter=verbose`\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- Did user-visible behavior change? No\n- Did config, environment, or migration behavior change? No\n- Did security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? No — tests only\n- Highest-risk area: none (test-only PR)\n- Mitigation: n/a\n\n## AI-assisted disclosure\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Cursor agent)\n- [x] Human-run Real behavior proof from local setup\n",
